    <string name="settings_fake_icmp">Answer ping locally</string>
    <string name="settings_fake_icmp_summary">Hysteria carries TCP and UDP only, so ICMP cannot pass. On, the tunnel answers ping itself: apps and games that check connectivity stay happy, but ping no longer tells you anything about the path.</string>
    <string name="settings_private_dns_hint">System Private DNS is on: names are resolved outside the tunnel, so this switch has no effect.</string>
    <string name="settings_dns_in_tunnel">Answer DNS in the tunnel</string>
    <string name="settings_dns_in_tunnel_summary">The tunnel answers names itself and forwards the name, so the server resolves it: no DNS round trip. Needs a working resolver on the server. Ignored while a custom DNS server is set.</string>
